WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:04.029
- She's a singer, songwriter,
actress, and filmmaker.

00:00:04.029 --> 00:00:07.302
She's one of the best selling
artists of all-time worldwide

00:00:07.302 --> 00:00:10.219
with over 245 million records sold.

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:14.167
She's the only recording artist
to have a number one album

00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:16.711
in each of the last six decades.

00:00:16.711 --> 00:00:18.120
She's Barbara Streisand,

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:21.703
and here are her top
ten rules for success.

00:00:23.935 --> 00:00:27.268
- A man's reach should exceed his grasp.

00:00:29.442 --> 00:00:31.942
It's just, life is a carousel,

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:36.575
life is a bowl of cherries,
I don't know it's,

00:00:36.575 --> 00:00:37.742
life is short.

00:00:40.794 --> 00:00:44.377
And you just got to
play, dance, experiment,

00:00:45.582 --> 00:00:47.832
fail, succeed, learn, give.

00:00:50.577 --> 00:00:54.494
In life it's like, you
know, follow your bliss.

00:00:56.361 --> 00:01:00.528
If you're following a path
that is pleasurable to you,

00:01:02.812 --> 00:01:05.062
it's much easier, it flows,

00:01:07.639 --> 00:01:10.404
there's a light behind the eyes you know.

00:01:10.404 --> 00:01:12.321
There's a shine within.

00:01:15.537 --> 00:01:19.704
It's beyond, it's not just
work, it's a joyous experience.

00:01:22.401 --> 00:01:24.091
You long for that.

00:01:24.091 --> 00:01:27.603
As I got older, I just thought,
how many people said to me,

00:01:27.603 --> 00:01:30.371
how could you not sing in
public, like we as your fans

00:01:30.371 --> 00:01:33.788
really want to hear you and see you live.

00:01:35.383 --> 00:01:38.830
And I thought, I owe this to them.

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:42.593
And maybe I owe it to myself
too to build up the courage

00:01:42.593 --> 00:01:45.681
to try it again, because
it's not about perfection,

00:01:45.681 --> 00:01:47.026
as you know, you know.

00:01:47.026 --> 00:01:49.479
This could happen, your
voice could go flat, dadada,

00:01:49.479 --> 00:01:51.329
and there is a certain excitement to that,

00:01:51.329 --> 00:01:55.496
and a certain acceptance again
of, you know, imperfections.

00:01:57.027 --> 00:01:59.166
My mother had a great voice.

00:01:59.166 --> 00:02:02.355
Not like mine, not like my
sister's, not like my son's.

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:05.083
A high soprano voice, but like a bird,

00:02:05.083 --> 00:02:07.583
I mean, really beautiful, but,

00:02:08.601 --> 00:02:11.621
I used to say mom, why didn't you try to

00:02:11.621 --> 00:02:13.229
get a career as a singer?

00:02:13.229 --> 00:02:15.996
No, she said she was too
shy, she couldn't do it.

00:02:15.996 --> 00:02:18.496
And I'm basically shy too, but

00:02:19.778 --> 00:02:21.801
that makes the difference, you know,

00:02:21.801 --> 00:02:24.178
how do you succeed if you don't try?

00:02:24.178 --> 00:02:25.645
The truth is, I think for years I thought,

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:27.895
well, I don't want to disappoint people.

00:02:27.895 --> 00:02:30.311
You know, it's like you
have this thing for me,

00:02:30.311 --> 00:02:32.944
well if you meet me, you know,
will you be disappointed,

00:02:32.944 --> 00:02:35.241
will it destroy the mystique?

00:02:35.241 --> 00:02:36.487
Now as you get older

00:02:36.487 --> 00:02:40.070
and when you accept
your own imperfections,

00:02:41.307 --> 00:02:42.458
there's a warmth to that,

00:02:42.458 --> 00:02:45.741
that's like the Indians sewing
in the flaw in the blanket,

00:02:45.741 --> 00:02:47.797
you know, that it shouldn't be perfect.

00:02:47.797 --> 00:02:50.165
So I really can't make a mistake,

00:02:50.165 --> 00:02:53.822
because if I accept my flaws,
then you will accept my flaws.

00:02:53.822 --> 00:02:54.655
- [Hostess] Exactly.

00:02:54.655 --> 00:02:55.572
- Music is,

00:02:57.843 --> 00:03:02.010
is transporting, music elevates
life, you know, music is

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:05.057
larger than life.

00:03:07.402 --> 00:03:11.025
You know, when you have certain emotions,

00:03:11.025 --> 00:03:13.554
that are larger than
life, you want to sing,

00:03:13.554 --> 00:03:17.647
you want to, you want to
express it in a larger way.

00:03:17.647 --> 00:03:20.397
Music is so powerful to the soul.

00:03:22.479 --> 00:03:26.646
It's so rich and being able
to identify with feelings.

00:03:30.433 --> 00:03:32.100
Music can transport.

00:03:34.017 --> 00:03:35.684
So it's very strong.

00:03:37.177 --> 00:03:38.010
- Did you have a lot of people

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:41.431
say you were never going to
make it besides your mom?

00:03:41.431 --> 00:03:42.692
- Yeah.

00:03:42.692 --> 00:03:43.722
- [Rosie] And what did
you think in your head

00:03:43.722 --> 00:03:45.472
when they'd say that?

00:03:46.534 --> 00:03:48.054
- I thought they were crazy.

00:03:48.054 --> 00:03:49.837
- Same thing with me, that's what I did.

00:03:49.837 --> 00:03:50.920
- (laughing) It's terrible.

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:53.712
No, I mean, I thought I
knew their, what meant,

00:03:53.712 --> 00:03:56.462
I knew why they thought that but,

00:03:57.584 --> 00:03:59.417
isn't that funny that

00:03:59.417 --> 00:04:03.197
within enormous insecurity and doubt,

00:04:03.197 --> 00:04:04.877
was a kind of a

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:05.710
- [Rosie] A knowing.

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:09.820
- A knowing that, you know
if I stick to my guns,

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:13.487
and I tell the truth
and I, I will be there,

00:04:14.433 --> 00:04:16.393
I don't know, I never
thought about it that much.

00:04:16.393 --> 00:04:19.993
It was something so deep I guess, that -

00:04:19.993 --> 00:04:21.971
I tell people, some
people ask me you know,

00:04:21.971 --> 00:04:24.412
do you think I should be an actress?

00:04:24.412 --> 00:04:26.794
And I say, boy, if you
have to think about it,

00:04:26.794 --> 00:04:27.714
don't be it.

00:04:27.714 --> 00:04:30.203
- Now I can direct,
people know I can direct,

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:32.286
now I can write songs, people
know I can write songs,

00:04:32.286 --> 00:04:33.675
I don't need to do that anymore?

00:04:33.675 --> 00:04:35.958
- I do bore myself a lot.

00:04:35.958 --> 00:04:39.672
You know I have to go on, and it's not

00:04:39.672 --> 00:04:41.941
conquer, I don't know if
I'd use the word conquer,

00:04:41.941 --> 00:04:44.858
it's, it's expanding one's horizon.

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:48.517
You know, it's trying something new.

00:04:48.517 --> 00:04:51.050
It's risking failure.

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:53.068
Even that's exciting to me.

00:04:53.068 --> 00:04:54.741
You see, actually you have to be

00:04:54.741 --> 00:04:57.749
thankful for people
like that 'cuz in a way,

00:04:57.749 --> 00:05:01.676
they gave you more courage,
they gave you more energy.

00:05:01.676 --> 00:05:04.910
More of a sense of your own destiny.

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:05.812
- It's true.

00:05:05.812 --> 00:05:10.220
- I thank my mother actually
for not believing in me.

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:12.325
Because I really set out to prove to her,

00:05:12.325 --> 00:05:16.228
that she was wrong, that I
could make something of my life,

00:05:16.228 --> 00:05:18.084
you know, as an actress.

00:05:18.084 --> 00:05:20.516
I am proud say I am.

00:05:20.516 --> 00:05:22.924
But there is no such thing as perfection,

00:05:22.924 --> 00:05:25.236
and I found that out
when I was 15 years old,

00:05:25.236 --> 00:05:27.196
I wrote it in my journal,

00:05:27.196 --> 00:05:30.372
that perfection is imperfection.

00:05:30.372 --> 00:05:33.789
So it has that humanity, a human quality.

00:05:34.724 --> 00:05:36.876
Otherwise it's too cold, right?

00:05:36.876 --> 00:05:39.292
You could just strive for perfection.

00:05:39.292 --> 00:05:43.247
Better word is excellence,
strive for excellence.

00:05:43.247 --> 00:05:44.688
